<title>FRANCE: Algeria seeks 100,000 tonnes wheat -traders.</title>
<headline>Algeria seeks 100,000 tonnes wheat -traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria has launched a new tender to import 100,000 tonnes of French or Argentine or U.S. milling wheat, or any combination of the three, for shipment in February and March, European grain traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>Exporters have until 1500 GMT on Monday to submit bids to sell in the tender, which was launched on Sunday, they said.  </p>
<p>The tender runs until Thursday, they said.</p>
<p>Algeria tendered last week to import 150,000 tonnes of milling wheat from French, or U.S., or Argentine origins for January and February shipment.</p>
<p>It ended up buying 50,000 tonnes of French wheat for January shipment at $172.50 per tonne, including freight and the cost of a Coface export credit, traders have said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
